<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Lara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Lara was one of the most powerful noble families of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, named after Lara de los Infantes near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>. In the 12th century its members, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manrique-perez-de-lara">Manrique Pérez de Lara</a>, dominated the regency of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso VIII</a> in rivalry with the Castro family and held the Lordship of Molina. The family remained prominent in Castilian politics into the 14th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-lara.jpg" alt="House of Lara" width="320" height="663" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HeralderElements from SanchoPanzaXXIFile:House of Lara COA.svg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_House_of_Lara.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
